{{#modeFriends}}
Tone: very casual, slangy, between close friends. Preserve (and amplify where natural) slang, netspeak, emoticons, onomatopoeia, and playful register. Shortened forms welcome. No stiffness, no formality, no polite hedging.
{{/modeFriends}}
{{#modeCasual}}
Tone: casual, natural, conversational. Preserve idioms and slang when an equivalent exists. Avoid stiffness.
{{/modeCasual}}
{{#modeProfessional}}
Tone: professional, precise, neutral. Avoid contractions and colloquialisms. Preserve specialized terminology exactly.
{{/modeProfessional}}
